Nmap Service Probes (service/nmap_fingerprints.py)
--------------------------------------------------

service/nmap_fingerprints.py contains a curated, normalized SUBSET of
service-detection fingerprints derived from Nmap's `nmap-service-probes`
database:

    Nmap Security Scanner - https://nmap.org
    Service probe data (C) 1998-2026 Insecure.Com LLC.
    Source revision: nmap-service-probes 39385 (2026-03-19)

This data is distributed under the Nmap Public Source License (NPSL):

    https://nmap.org/npsl/

The fingerprints in service/nmap_fingerprints.py are a modified subset:
selected common services only, converted from Nmap's PCRE syntax to
Python `re` byte patterns, with only the service name, pattern and
product/version templates retained. This is NOT the official Nmap
database, and TCPrax is not affiliated with or endorsed by the Nmap
Project. The generated file is marked with source="nmap-service-probes"
on every entry so its origin is traceable in code.

To regenerate this file from a local copy of nmap-service-probes:

    python3 tools/extract_nmap_fingerprints.py [path/to/nmap-service-probes]


IANA Service Names and Port Numbers
-----------------------------------

TCPrax's common-service dataset and port hints are based on the service
name and port number assignments published by IANA in the Service Name
and Transport Protocol Port Number Registry:

    https://www.iana.org/assignments/service-names-port-numbers/

Port and service-name assignments are factual registrations. IANA does
NOT publish or endorse any "most common services" ranking; TCPrax's
selection of common services is a curated dataset based on IANA
registrations supplemented by public service-usage data, and is
described as such (see README). IANA data is used for identification
hints only, never as sole proof that a service is running on a port.
